<title>USA: Sri Lanka seen seeking 100,000 T optional wheat.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka seen seeking 100,000 T optional wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka is expected to tender on October 18 for 100,000 tonnes optional origin wheat, U.S. traders said.</p>
<p>Out of the total, 50,000 tonnes would be soft white wheat and 50,000 tonnes hard red winter wheat.</p>
<p>Shipment is slated for November 11-20.</p>
<p>--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305</p>
